{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is there not a warfare to man upon earth?\nAnd are not his days like the days of a hireling?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As a servant that earnestly desireth the shadow,\nAnd as a hireling that looketh for his wages:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So am I made to possess months of misery,\nAnd wearisome nights are appointed to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I lie down, I say,\nWhen shall I arise, and the night be gone?\nAnd I am full of tossings to and fro unto the dawning of the day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My flesh is clothed with worms and clods of dust;\nMy skin closeth up, and breaketh out afresh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My days are swifter than a weaver’s shuttle,\nAnd are spent without hope.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh remember that my life is a breath:\nMine eye shall no more see good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The eye of him that seeth me shall behold me no more;\nThine eyes shall be upon me, but I shall not be.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As the cloud is consumed and vanisheth away,\nSo he that goeth down to Sheol shall come up no more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall return no more to his house,\nNeither shall his place know him any more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I will not refrain my mouth;\nI will speak in the anguish of my spirit;\nI will complain in the bitterness of my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Am I a sea, or a sea-monster,\nThat thou settest a watch over me?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I say, My bed shall comfort me,\nMy couch shall ease my complaint;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then thou scarest me with dreams,\nAnd terrifiest me through visions:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So that my soul chooseth strangling,\nAnd death rather than ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my bones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I loathe ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my life",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; I would not live alway:\nLet me alone; for my days are vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What is man, that thou shouldest magnify him,\nAnd that thou shouldest set thy mind upon him,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And that thou shouldest visit him every morning,\nAnd try him every moment?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How long wilt thou not look away from me,\nNor let me alone till I swallow down my spittle?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have sinned, what do I unto thee, O thou watcher of men?\nWhy hast thou set me as a mark for thee,\nSo that I am a burden to myself?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.7.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And why dost thou not pardon my transgression, and take away mine iniquity?\nFor now shall I lie down in the dust;\nAnd thou wilt seek me diligently, but I shall not be.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
